[[:db/retract 17592186152792 :question/answer-fields 17592186151259] {:db/id 17592186152097 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e91f8fe9-c6f2-558a-bf39-b0389019d5ff" "question-44e36839-2675-57c4-abf9-91a0b0717003" "question-abd84654-ac2d-58a6-9574-529f2b4aa6f5" "question-a55de8de-5dbf-5007-a3cb-517652d485f3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151846 :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[5]_{8}?$\n\n- $-3$\n\n- $13$\n\n- $3$" :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[5]_{8}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $5$ modulo $8.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[5]_{8} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=5+8k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={5+8k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,5-2\\cdot 8,\\,5-8,\\,5,\\,5+8,\\,5+2\\cdot 8,\\,…} \\\\  & ={…,-11,-3,5,13,21,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-3$ and $13$ belong to $[5]_{8},$ while $3$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152098 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4eec4737-7c33-5f5e-94da-8528e3f19d9b" "question-9486abbb-c811-54ba-bf39-16141b4e8ba4" "question-476816fb-a049-55c8-86b3-04683cf8a95e" "question-9c32efaa-b6d9-5d28-a23f-80c818eab9ef" "question-d1a9f6cf-cd8d-55d6-a82c-4176e7807557"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151847 :question/problem "Which of the following residue classes modulo $3$ contain the integer $7?$\n\n- $[4]_3$\n\n- $[-1]_3$\n\n- $[1]_3$" :question/worked-solution "We have $7 \\in [a]_{3}$ if \n\n$$\n7 \\equiv a \\quad (\\text{mod}\\:3).\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $7 \\in [4]_3$ because $7 \\equiv 4 \\: (\\text{mod}\\:3)$ $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- $7 \\not\\in [-1]_3$ because $7 \\not\\equiv -1 \\: (\\text{mod}\\:3)$ $\\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n\n- $7 \\in [1]_3$ because $7 \\equiv 1 \\: (\\text{mod}\\:3)$ $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152099 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6ec8e64f-343c-590b-a372-9757c285ca4e" "question-c46ee0cd-65d1-59a8-92bc-e1fc2e8dbb10" "question-0c2846ce-57fa-59ad-9fe2-ab1c6ed9c653" "question-1bd78006-ade4-5556-a33a-5b5262685fbe" "question-06e706ec-ef55-5e4d-a1fb-e7ced3a44078"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151848 :question/problem "If $[a]_n$ denotes the residue class containing all integers congruent to $a$ modulo $n,$ then which of the following residue classes is equal to $[13]_3?$\n\n- $[0]_3$\n\n- $[1]_3$\n\n- $[2]_3$" :question/worked-solution "We have $[a]_{3} = [b]_{3}$ if \n\n$$\na \\equiv b \\quad (\\text{mod}\\:3).\n$$\n\nThe residue class $[13]_{3}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $13$ modulo $3.$ \n\nWe can find an alternative representation for this residue class as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[13]_{3} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡13\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡4\\cdot 3+1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡4\\cdot 0+1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)} \\\\  & =[1]_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152100 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f68491fc-7fbf-551d-bb56-21bac80c159f" "question-0f9012f2-83ba-5f6f-b553-2ea47d5d4f81" "question-b83f0a5d-69e2-5527-92eb-107f538fccca" "question-32f1fbfd-ebfc-5a37-bf9e-b69da2b29724" "question-82a421fb-21ef-5dca-a27b-abed22994846"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151850 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- There are $4$ distinct residue classes modulo $8$\n\n- $[5]_{3} \\cap [9]_{3} = \\emptyset$\n\n- $\\mathbb{Z} = [4]_{3} \\cup [5]_{3} \\cup [9]_{3}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_n \\cap [b]_n = \\emptyset$ if $a \\not\\equiv b \\: (\\text{mod}\\:n)$\n\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: \n\n$$\n\\mathbb{Z} = [0]_n \\cup [1]_n \\cup \\cdots \\cup [n-1]_n\n$$\n\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: \n\n$$\n\\mathbb{Z}_n = \\big\\{[0]_n,\\, [1]_n,\\, \\ldots,\\,  [n-1]_n\\big\\}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. There are exactly $8$ distinct residue classes modulo $8.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $5 \\not\\equiv 9 \\: (\\text{mod }3),$ we have that $[5]_3\\cap [9]_3= \\emptyset.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[4]_{3} & =[1+3\\cdot 1]_{3}=[1]_{3} \\\\ [5]_{3} & =[2+3\\cdot 1]_{3}=[2]_{3} \\\\ [9]_{3} & =[0+3\\cdot 3]_{3}=[0]_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[4]_{3}\\cup [5]_{3}\\cup [9]_{3} & =[1]_{3}\\cup [2]_{3}\\cup [0]_{3} \\\\  & =[0]_{3}\\cup [1]_{3}\\cup [2]_{3} \\\\  & =Z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-e91f8fe9-c6f2-558a-bf39-b0389019d5ff" :question/id #uuid "e91f8fe9-c6f2-558a-bf39-b0389019d5ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-86021" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[7]_{11}?$\n\n- $18$\n- $-4$\n- $15$" :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[7]_{11}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $7$ modulo $11.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[7]_{11} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=7+11k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={7+11k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,7-2\\cdot 11,\\,7-11,\\,7,\\,7+11,\\,7+2\\cdot 11,…} \\\\  & ={…,-15,-4,7,18,29,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-4$ and $18$ belong to $[7]_{11},$ while $15$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f2e9f81c-9578-565c-8322-3231a43ad273"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f2e9f81c-9578-565c-8322-3231a43ad273" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2e9f81c-9578-565c-8322-3231a43ad273" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-16580a0c-365e-59a9-9828-bb02a47e8573" :answer-field/choices ["answer-16580a0c-365e-59a9-9828-bb02a47e8573" "answer-7e33db2a-1dbd-5414-9540-709392a7913f" "answer-c638689c-94e7-5af8-b84c-75a738f6395e" "answer-abb17be0-afe8-5a6d-8ef7-96917a6efd85" "answer-b9bdbd57-ea56-5ecb-8fe2-07753e9011a5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16580a0c-365e-59a9-9828-bb02a47e8573" :answer/id #uuid "16580a0c-365e-59a9-9828-bb02a47e8573" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e33db2a-1dbd-5414-9540-709392a7913f" :answer/id #uuid "7e33db2a-1dbd-5414-9540-709392a7913f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c638689c-94e7-5af8-b84c-75a738f6395e" :answer/id #uuid "c638689c-94e7-5af8-b84c-75a738f6395e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abb17be0-afe8-5a6d-8ef7-96917a6efd85" :answer/id #uuid "abb17be0-afe8-5a6d-8ef7-96917a6efd85" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9bdbd57-ea56-5ecb-8fe2-07753e9011a5" :answer/id #uuid "b9bdbd57-ea56-5ecb-8fe2-07753e9011a5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-44e36839-2675-57c4-abf9-91a0b0717003" :question/id #uuid "44e36839-2675-57c4-abf9-91a0b0717003" :question/math-academy-id "q-214450" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[4]_{7}?$\n\n- $-3$\n- $6$\n- $18$" :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[4]_{7}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $4$ modulo $7.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[4]_{7} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=4+7k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={4+7k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,4-2\\cdot 7,\\,4-7,\\,4,\\,4+7,\\,4+2\\cdot 7,\\,…} \\\\  & ={…,-10,-3,4,11,18,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-3$ and $18$ belong to $[4]_{7},$ while $6$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-86eeeda2-7dc4-5dc4-b9bd-b1e07b0c7e13"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-86eeeda2-7dc4-5dc4-b9bd-b1e07b0c7e13" :answer-field/id #uuid "86eeeda2-7dc4-5dc4-b9bd-b1e07b0c7e13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a3be6687-8c01-58a1-8b6f-55c990a13f73" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ddf198f1-51ce-5197-901f-4a57ec6ca534" "answer-a3be6687-8c01-58a1-8b6f-55c990a13f73" "answer-536a2ad9-31ea-58bb-ad50-9a311d120bc0" "answer-2ae50f18-3a44-5059-859d-62a308e0626c" "answer-6e813eca-88bc-51a0-a774-be6fb12da67f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ddf198f1-51ce-5197-901f-4a57ec6ca534" :answer/id #uuid "ddf198f1-51ce-5197-901f-4a57ec6ca534" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3be6687-8c01-58a1-8b6f-55c990a13f73" :answer/id #uuid "a3be6687-8c01-58a1-8b6f-55c990a13f73" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-536a2ad9-31ea-58bb-ad50-9a311d120bc0" :answer/id #uuid "536a2ad9-31ea-58bb-ad50-9a311d120bc0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ae50f18-3a44-5059-859d-62a308e0626c" :answer/id #uuid "2ae50f18-3a44-5059-859d-62a308e0626c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e813eca-88bc-51a0-a774-be6fb12da67f" :answer/id #uuid "6e813eca-88bc-51a0-a774-be6fb12da67f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-abd84654-ac2d-58a6-9574-529f2b4aa6f5" :question/id #uuid "abd84654-ac2d-58a6-9574-529f2b4aa6f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-78597" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[-7]_{11}?$\n\n- $15$\n- $-4$\n- $7$" :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[-7]_{11}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $-7$ modulo $11.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[-7]_{11} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡-7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=-7+11k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={-7+11k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,-7-2\\cdot 11,\\,-7-11,\\,-7,\\,-7+11,\\,-7+2\\cdot 11,\\,…} \\\\  & ={…,-29,-18,-7,4,15,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $15$ belongs to $[-7]_{11},$ while $-4$ and $7$ do not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-99eba53e-9c7a-538e-95be-f63aec7390ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-99eba53e-9c7a-538e-95be-f63aec7390ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "99eba53e-9c7a-538e-95be-f63aec7390ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c2eeae29-6589-5372-9208-8579d86384ca" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2d6e5a94-ee4d-53e1-8683-a2c6015c7c95" "answer-fc4562a3-8e24-54b7-820d-6e3b72017105" "answer-c2eeae29-6589-5372-9208-8579d86384ca" "answer-5479ed01-e1d6-5e5a-b01f-9abefb2c6a10" "answer-c8b963dd-bb5a-5a02-9158-70da5aa07a71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d6e5a94-ee4d-53e1-8683-a2c6015c7c95" :answer/id #uuid "2d6e5a94-ee4d-53e1-8683-a2c6015c7c95" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc4562a3-8e24-54b7-820d-6e3b72017105" :answer/id #uuid "fc4562a3-8e24-54b7-820d-6e3b72017105" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2eeae29-6589-5372-9208-8579d86384ca" :answer/id #uuid "c2eeae29-6589-5372-9208-8579d86384ca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5479ed01-e1d6-5e5a-b01f-9abefb2c6a10" :answer/id #uuid "5479ed01-e1d6-5e5a-b01f-9abefb2c6a10" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8b963dd-bb5a-5a02-9158-70da5aa07a71" :answer/id #uuid "c8b963dd-bb5a-5a02-9158-70da5aa07a71" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a55de8de-5dbf-5007-a3cb-517652d485f3" :question/id #uuid "a55de8de-5dbf-5007-a3cb-517652d485f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-78599" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[9]_{13}?$\n\n- $4$\n- $-17$\n- $35$" :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[9]_{13}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $9$ modulo $13.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[9]_{13} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡9\\,(\\text{mod}\\,13)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=9+13k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={9+13k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,9-2\\cdot 13,\\,9-13,\\,9,\\,9+13,\\,9+2\\cdot 13,\\,…} \\\\  & ={…,-17,-4,9,22,35,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-17$ and $35$ belong to $[9]_{13},$ while $4$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f4475c97-7935-5890-8ef0-c7a0d0f183f4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f4475c97-7935-5890-8ef0-c7a0d0f183f4" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4475c97-7935-5890-8ef0-c7a0d0f183f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d22c7286-cdcb-5191-9d60-a9974ca672d6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-14030e88-6395-56f9-82ae-0053228a0a90" "answer-d73fae85-da65-51ae-ad7a-ae836d3b1e11" "answer-a892cb8e-e16a-5a18-b277-91ca8afd57cc" "answer-d22c7286-cdcb-5191-9d60-a9974ca672d6" "answer-8ed69294-b796-5762-a670-e84ffa5fce8c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14030e88-6395-56f9-82ae-0053228a0a90" :answer/id #uuid "14030e88-6395-56f9-82ae-0053228a0a90" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d73fae85-da65-51ae-ad7a-ae836d3b1e11" :answer/id #uuid "d73fae85-da65-51ae-ad7a-ae836d3b1e11" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a892cb8e-e16a-5a18-b277-91ca8afd57cc" :answer/id #uuid "a892cb8e-e16a-5a18-b277-91ca8afd57cc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d22c7286-cdcb-5191-9d60-a9974ca672d6" :answer/id #uuid "d22c7286-cdcb-5191-9d60-a9974ca672d6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ed69294-b796-5762-a670-e84ffa5fce8c" :answer/id #uuid "8ed69294-b796-5762-a670-e84ffa5fce8c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152792 :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[6]_{9}?$\n\n- $-12$\n- $3$\n- $24$" :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[6]_{9}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $6$ modulo $9.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[6]_{9} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡6\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=6+9k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={6+9k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,6-2\\cdot 9,\\,6-9,\\,6,\\,6+9,\\,6+2\\cdot 9,\\,…} \\\\  & ={…,-12,-3,6,15,24,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-12$ and $24$ belong to $[6]_{9},$ while $3$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cce84edd-038c-58d1-9051-41a39c1a5bad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cce84edd-038c-58d1-9051-41a39c1a5bad" :answer-field/id #uuid "cce84edd-038c-58d1-9051-41a39c1a5bad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8508cb49-93b9-537a-b130-be5b95ed2386" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c35aa81f-3a6b-57fc-9666-5deb89ff8dcc" "answer-8508cb49-93b9-537a-b130-be5b95ed2386" "answer-6ef83927-2628-5d68-bf65-a48c1fe20d5c" "answer-88959a9d-340f-5ee1-b746-8a0de81e8b1d" "answer-1033dd79-9600-51c4-a8ca-3a31c3dde48f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c35aa81f-3a6b-57fc-9666-5deb89ff8dcc" :answer/id #uuid "c35aa81f-3a6b-57fc-9666-5deb89ff8dcc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8508cb49-93b9-537a-b130-be5b95ed2386" :answer/id #uuid "8508cb49-93b9-537a-b130-be5b95ed2386" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ef83927-2628-5d68-bf65-a48c1fe20d5c" :answer/id #uuid "6ef83927-2628-5d68-bf65-a48c1fe20d5c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88959a9d-340f-5ee1-b746-8a0de81e8b1d" :answer/id #uuid "88959a9d-340f-5ee1-b746-8a0de81e8b1d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1033dd79-9600-51c4-a8ca-3a31c3dde48f" :answer/id #uuid "1033dd79-9600-51c4-a8ca-3a31c3dde48f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4eec4737-7c33-5f5e-94da-8528e3f19d9b" :question/id #uuid "4eec4737-7c33-5f5e-94da-8528e3f19d9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-86030" :question/problem "Which of the following residue classes modulo $5$ contain the integer $-7?$\n\n- $[-2]_{5}$\n- $[3]_{5}$\n- $[7]_{5}$" :question/worked-solution "We have $-7\\in [a]_{5}$ if \n\n$$\n-7≡a\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5).\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $-7\\in [-2]_{5}$ because $-7≡-2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ $\\,✓$\n\n- $-7\\in [3]_{5}$ because $-7≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ $\\,✓$\n\n- $-7\\notin [7]_{5}$ because $-7≢7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-42399fdd-171f-5d3c-8ecb-541580d44e17"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-42399fdd-171f-5d3c-8ecb-541580d44e17" :answer-field/id #uuid "42399fdd-171f-5d3c-8ecb-541580d44e17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-575da76a-a021-573e-9647-5cecb1252317" :answer-field/choices ["answer-575da76a-a021-573e-9647-5cecb1252317" "answer-def92c9e-e6e2-5c8e-91e7-4b7fb21509ef" "answer-cf29b9c2-05c6-5263-a0ab-8a4e2db19757" "answer-90050eab-d210-5e6f-ab25-dd473065930c" "answer-141ec379-3ffa-52e6-bad6-ca1691d2141a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-575da76a-a021-573e-9647-5cecb1252317" :answer/id #uuid "575da76a-a021-573e-9647-5cecb1252317" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-def92c9e-e6e2-5c8e-91e7-4b7fb21509ef" :answer/id #uuid "def92c9e-e6e2-5c8e-91e7-4b7fb21509ef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf29b9c2-05c6-5263-a0ab-8a4e2db19757" :answer/id #uuid "cf29b9c2-05c6-5263-a0ab-8a4e2db19757" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90050eab-d210-5e6f-ab25-dd473065930c" :answer/id #uuid "90050eab-d210-5e6f-ab25-dd473065930c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-141ec379-3ffa-52e6-bad6-ca1691d2141a" :answer/id #uuid "141ec379-3ffa-52e6-bad6-ca1691d2141a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9486abbb-c811-54ba-bf39-16141b4e8ba4" :question/id #uuid "9486abbb-c811-54ba-bf39-16141b4e8ba4" :question/math-academy-id "q-86026" :question/problem "Which of the following residue classes modulo $8$ contain the integer $5?$\n\n- $[-3]_{8}$\n- $[13]_{8}$\n- $[6]_{8}$" :question/worked-solution "We have $5\\in [a]_{8}$ if \n\n$$\n5≡a\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $5\\in [-3]_{8}$ because $5≡-3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$ $\\,✓$\n\n- $5\\in [13]_{8}$ because $5≡13\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$ $\\,✓$\n\n- $5\\notin [6]_{8}$ because $5≢6\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-efe5acad-f997-5276-8d8a-e17aaf71a1b3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-efe5acad-f997-5276-8d8a-e17aaf71a1b3" :answer-field/id #uuid "efe5acad-f997-5276-8d8a-e17aaf71a1b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3ef56e58-353f-5a33-bde3-a2b6e4c4903e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3ef56e58-353f-5a33-bde3-a2b6e4c4903e" "answer-aac3d64f-1456-56de-acb9-9bfb8ecbd046" "answer-b15383af-255e-5472-96e9-e1358bbfd80b" "answer-c0af28c5-30e3-5b6d-88e9-06e26645efe2" "answer-a9891a5c-4a6c-5224-86ee-155e6eb8d9cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ef56e58-353f-5a33-bde3-a2b6e4c4903e" :answer/id #uuid "3ef56e58-353f-5a33-bde3-a2b6e4c4903e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aac3d64f-1456-56de-acb9-9bfb8ecbd046" :answer/id #uuid "aac3d64f-1456-56de-acb9-9bfb8ecbd046" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1538