d "81087f72-4918-5614-9cfb-be935bd74663" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c5856a96-f7b4-5c0c-8c44-8b6c81d37607" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c27ce301-a593-5534-a045-c8e23fc79bb0" "answer-a7d1238b-22f5-51bf-ad99-330fde0e0432" "answer-e468ea16-7d58-5381-9c3e-97010cf5f55b" "answer-c5856a96-f7b4-5c0c-8c44-8b6c81d37607" "answer-4c2050fc-dd72-59da-bd00-d4fb4787ba45"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c27ce301-a593-5534-a045-c8e23fc79bb0" :answer/id #uuid "c27ce301-a593-5534-a045-c8e23fc79bb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[0]_{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7d1238b-22f5-51bf-ad99-330fde0e0432" :answer/id #uuid "a7d1238b-22f5-51bf-ad99-330fde0e0432" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[1]_{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e468ea16-7d58-5381-9c3e-97010cf5f55b" :answer/id #uuid "e468ea16-7d58-5381-9c3e-97010cf5f55b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[2]_{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5856a96-f7b4-5c0c-8c44-8b6c81d37607" :answer/id #uuid "c5856a96-f7b4-5c0c-8c44-8b6c81d37607" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[4]_{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c2050fc-dd72-59da-bd00-d4fb4787ba45" :answer/id #uuid "4c2050fc-dd72-59da-bd00-d4fb4787ba45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[5]_{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1bd78006-ade4-5556-a33a-5b5262685fbe" :question/id #uuid "1bd78006-ade4-5556-a33a-5b5262685fbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-86035" :question/problem "If $[a]_{n}$ denotes the residue class containing all integers congruent to $a$ modulo $n,$ then $[-13]_{5}=$" :question/worked-solution "We have $[a]_{5}=[b]_{5}$ if \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5).\n$$\n\nThe residue class $[-13]_{5}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $-13$ modulo $5.$ \n\nWe can find an alternative representation for this residue class as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[-13]_{5} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡-13\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡(-3)\\cdot 5+2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡(-3)\\cdot 0+2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)} \\\\  & =[2]_{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d321d184-ce8b-5544-8e0b-4c7fd57a0a98"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d321d184-ce8b-5544-8e0b-4c7fd57a0a98" :answer-field/id #uuid "d321d184-ce8b-5544-8e0b-4c7fd57a0a98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-952759eb-0e3e-5800-ac84-bf79ec646ecf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0636d430-5e30-5d21-8647-9ba69f94907c" "answer-e37f517a-1c00-5080-a17b-5cfdbbd2da1a" "answer-952759eb-0e3e-5800-ac84-bf79ec646ecf" "answer-cc197bf1-e9bb-5eeb-be5f-93b0c73c79b2" "answer-3ebbd4db-2968-5f79-8339-3f181b9aa536"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0636d430-5e30-5d21-8647-9ba69f94907c" :answer/id #uuid "0636d430-5e30-5d21-8647-9ba69f94907c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[0]_{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e37f517a-1c00-5080-a17b-5cfdbbd2da1a" :answer/id #uuid "e37f517a-1c00-5080-a17b-5cfdbbd2da1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[1]_{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-952759eb-0e3e-5800-ac84-bf79ec646ecf" :answer/id #uuid "952759eb-0e3e-5800-ac84-bf79ec646ecf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[2]_{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc197bf1-e9bb-5eeb-be5f-93b0c73c79b2" :answer/id #uuid "cc197bf1-e9bb-5eeb-be5f-93b0c73c79b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[3]_{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ebbd4db-2968-5f79-8339-3f181b9aa536" :answer/id #uuid "3ebbd4db-2968-5f79-8339-3f181b9aa536" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[4]_{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-06e706ec-ef55-5e4d-a1fb-e7ced3a44078" :question/id #uuid "06e706ec-ef55-5e4d-a1fb-e7ced3a44078" :question/math-academy-id "q-86034" :question/problem "If $[a]_{n}$ denotes the residue class containing all integers congruent to $a$ modulo $n,$ then $[-21]_{6}=$" :question/worked-solution "We have $[a]_{6}=[b]_{6}$ if \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6).\n$$\n\nThe residue class $[-21]_{6}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $-21$ modulo $6.$ \n\nWe can find an alternative representation for this residue class as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[-21]_{6} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡-21\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡(-4)\\cdot 6+3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡(-4)\\cdot 0+3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)} \\\\  & =[3]_{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3107f40f-9ecd-5896-b96d-bd32cac730cd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3107f40f-9ecd-5896-b96d-bd32cac730cd" :answer-field/id #uuid "3107f40f-9ecd-5896-b96d-bd32cac730cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-03d0960c-af61-5116-9326-54622ce4d65f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-579fee27-e1b5-5dfd-851e-08154afab314" "answer-77d4339d-48cc-5e13-9ad6-28908953770a" "answer-03d0960c-af61-5116-9326-54622ce4d65f" "answer-d0255b94-ede3-5ce4-bb10-56451be8a87e" "answer-961ca45e-d10a-5051-97be-d9e6f717d64f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-579fee27-e1b5-5dfd-851e-08154afab314" :answer/id #uuid "579fee27-e1b5-5dfd-851e-08154afab314" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[0]_{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77d4339d-48cc-5e13-9ad6-28908953770a" :answer/id #uuid "77d4339d-48cc-5e13-9ad6-28908953770a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[2]_{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03d0960c-af61-5116-9326-54622ce4d65f" :answer/id #uuid "03d0960c-af61-5116-9326-54622ce4d65f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[3]_{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0255b94-ede3-5ce4-bb10-56451be8a87e" :answer/id #uuid "d0255b94-ede3-5ce4-bb10-56451be8a87e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[4]_{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-961ca45e-d10a-5051-97be-d9e6f717d64f" :answer/id #uuid "961ca45e-d10a-5051-97be-d9e6f717d64f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[5]_{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f68491fc-7fbf-551d-bb56-21bac80c159f" :question/id #uuid "f68491fc-7fbf-551d-bb56-21bac80c159f" :question/math-academy-id "q-78644" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- There are $11$ distinct residue classes modulo $11$\n- $[7]_{5}\\cap [2]_{5}\\ne ∅$\n- $Z=[0]_{4}\\cup [9]_{4}\\cup [2]_{4}\\cup [15]_{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_{n}\\cap [b]_{n}=∅$ if $a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: \n\n$$\nZ=[0]_{n}\\cup [1]_{n}\\cup ⋯\\cup [n-1]_{n}\n$$\n\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: \n\n$$\n{Z}_{n}={[0]_{n},\\,[1]_{n},\\,…,\\,[n-1]_{n}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. There are $11$ distinct residue classes modulo $11.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $7≡2\\,(\\text{mod }5),$ we have that $[7]_{5}=[2]_{5}.$ Therefore, $[7]_{5}\\cap [2]_{5}\\ne ∅.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[9]_{4} & =[1+4\\cdot 2]_{4}=[1]_{4} \\\\ [15]_{4} & =[3+4\\cdot 3]_{4}=[3]_{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[0]_{4}\\cup [9]_{4}\\cup [2]_{4}\\cup [15]_{4} & =[0]_{4}\\cup [1]_{4}\\cup [2]_{4}\\cup [3]_{4} \\\\  & =Z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0dd3a9af-e1c5-54e0-8441-f550817b9384"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0dd3a9af-e1c5-54e0-8441-f550817b9384" :answer-field/id #uuid "0dd3a9af-e1c5-54e0-8441-f550817b9384" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ccfb74cf-ee0e-514f-afc8-cbb35b8f9393" :answer-field/choices ["answer-52eadcaf-a11c-568b-907e-2ff81396dc49" "answer-406d20f8-1407-5435-8784-5f3e29ff681c" "answer-7ecfdc45-6d9f-55e1-936c-36ea7836a224" "answer-ccfb74cf-ee0e-514f-afc8-cbb35b8f9393" "answer-4a92891f-39e5-5cee-b46a-8784882f23fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52eadcaf-a11c-568b-907e-2ff81396dc49" :answer/id #uuid "52eadcaf-a11c-568b-907e-2ff81396dc49" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-406d20f8-1407-5435-8784-5f3e29ff681c" :answer/id #uuid "406d20f8-1407-5435-8784-5f3e29ff681c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ecfdc45-6d9f-55e1-936c-36ea7836a224" :answer/id #uuid "7ecfdc45-6d9f-55e1-936c-36ea7836a224" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ccfb74cf-ee0e-514f-afc8-cbb35b8f9393" :answer/id #uuid "ccfb74cf-ee0e-514f-afc8-cbb35b8f9393" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a92891f-39e5-5cee-b46a-8784882f23fc" :answer/id #uuid "4a92891f-39e5-5cee-b46a-8784882f23fc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0f9012f2-83ba-5f6f-b553-2ea47d5d4f81" :question/id #uuid "0f9012f2-83ba-5f6f-b553-2ea47d5d4f81" :question/math-academy-id "q-78640" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- There are $3$ distinct residue classes modulo $6$\n- $[5]_{3}\\cap [1]_{3}\\ne ∅$\n- $Z=[3]_{2}\\cup [6]_{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_{n}\\cap [b]_{n}=∅$ if $a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: \n\n$$\nZ=[0]_{n}\\cup [1]_{n}\\cup ⋯\\cup [n-1]_{n}\n$$\n\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: \n\n$$\n{Z}_{n}={[0]_{n},\\,[1]_{n},\\,…,\\,[n-1]_{n}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. There are exactly $6$ distinct residue classes modulo $6.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $5≢1\\,(\\text{mod }3),$ we have that $[5]_{3}\\cap [1]_{3}=∅.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[3]_{2} & =[1+2\\cdot 1]_{2}=[1]_{2} \\\\ [6]_{2} & =[0+2\\cdot 3]_{2}=[0]_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[3]_{2}\\cup [6]_{2} & =[1]_{2}\\cup [0]_{2} \\\\  & =[0]_{2}\\cup [1]_{2} \\\\  & =Z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2372040f-636b-51db-a88a-0a20d411e932"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2372040f-636b-51db-a88a-0a20d411e932" :answer-field/id #uuid "2372040f-636b-51db-a88a-0a20d411e932" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c31a23b5-9755-5c42-94ff-b6938dbd6b75" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5f50b178-baf5-50bc-b791-e2b9c9ce601d" "answer-7ba5e226-5ed0-5aa6-8f25-569b9054ddde" "answer-2a74b48c-8a09-5420-9014-3039dfa3